 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Start with an idea, not a final drawing. Make notes and rough sketches, jump from one to the next without finishing, and don't draw the lines straight up. That's okay. Let yourself draw really badly. A sketchbook full of bad drawings is better than one empty one. Draw cafes and shops stay wide awake in them. Sit somewhere you'd normally finish your coffee, and use people watching as inspiration. It is, and that's the point. The weirder you look, the more people will leave you alone. A sketchbook for drawing, a bag for drawings, and a deadline give your drawings purpose.",
